  data: {
    LLM: 'Game: Lame Brain Pete. Logic: 3 hole cards, 4 community cards revealed sequentially. Wild card = lowest rank among all 4 community cards (determined after 4th card). Betting rounds after hole cards and after each community card. Standard poker hand evaluation with wild cards.',
    Player: "Welcome to Lame Brain Pete. You'll get three hole cards and watch four community cards appear one by one. But here's the twistâ€”the lowest card showing on the board becomes wild at the end. Will your hand improve or fall apart? Bet wisely and remember: in this game, patience is often rewarded.",
    objective: 'Form the best five-card poker hand using any combination of your three hole cards and the four community cards.',
    gameplay: '1. **Ante**: All players post an ante. 2. **Initial Deal**: Each player receives 3 hole cards. 3. **First Betting Round**: Players bet based on their hole cards only. 4. **First Community Card**: Dealer reveals the first community card face-up. This is NOT automatically wild. 5. **Second Betting Round**: Players bet. 6. **Second Community Card**: Revealed. 7. **Third Betting Round**: Players bet. 8. **Third Community Card**: Revealed. 9. **Fourth Betting Round**: Players bet. 10. **Fourth Community Card**: Revealed. 11. **Final Betting Round**: Players bet. 12. **Showdown**: Remaining players reveal hands.',
    keyRules: [
      'The wild card is determined only after ALL four community cards are revealed.',
      'Until the final card, players must speculate on what the wild card might be.',
      'Standard poker hand rankings apply, with wild cards substituting for any rank/suit.',
      'If two community cards tie for lowest rank, both ranks are wild.',
      'Aces are high for determining the lowest wild card.',
    ],
